---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { practiceClaims, siteFacts } from '../data/site-facts';
---

<Layout title="Yoga | Amitoj Singh" description="A personal practice of attention, effort, and release through the body.">
  <section class="container-zen pt-8 md:pt-12 pb-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <img
        src="/images/photography-optimized/DSCF1773.webp"
        alt="A thin branch against a softly blurred orange and gray background"
        class="practice-hero"
        width="1600"
        height="1066"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-zen section-zen pt-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted mb-3">{practiceClaims.router.yoga.label}</p>
      <h1 class="mb-6 text-balance">Yoga</h1>
      <div class="accent-line mb-8"></div>
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-light mb-6">{practiceClaims.yogaMethod}</p>
      <p class="text-ink-light">I have practiced for {siteFacts.yogaPractice}. What began as physical exercise became a way of studying attention.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-zen section-zen border-t border-oat-300">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl mb-6 section-header">Practice</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-light mb-6">Attention is easier to describe than to sustain. In yoga, effort provides an immediate test: am I still attending to what is happening, or only trying to produce the next position?</p>
      <p class="text-ink-light">The practice does not settle what to do. It makes the quality of attention harder to hide.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-zen section-zen border-t border-oat-300">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl mb-6 section-header">A local connection</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-light mb-6">The working theory on this site asks how awareness and agency can remain joined as more cognition becomes delegable. Yoga contributes one local observation: attention is not only cognitive. It is also embodied.</p>
      <a href="/third-enlightenment" class="arrow-link">Read the working theory</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-zen section-zen border-t border-oat-300">
    <a href="/practices" class="arrow-link">All practices</a>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .practice-hero {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 28rem;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 55%;
  }
</style>
